      "date": "2026-11-22 12:55:38.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. The dummy-slot repair for EC data stripes does not seem to give the result the patch describes. test_56 only checks for the \"hole\" pattern on an empty file. Could it write data first and then read it back with cmp, and also run `lfs mirror resync`, after LFSCK has repaired the file? That would exercise the parity rebuild this repair depends on.",
