          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-22 05:35:02.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20911 lfsck: check the layout of EC files",
        "message": "LU-20911 lfsck: check the layout of EC files\n\nLFSCK only accepted the layout of an EC file, with its parity\ncomponents, when it rebuilt it from orphan OST objects.  Its scans\nskipped EC files, and when an OST with lfsck_verify_pfid enabled asked\nthe MDT to verify an EC object whose parent FID or stripe index did\nnot match the RPC, the MDT refused it, so the OST kept returning\n-EINPROGRESS and the client resent the I/O forever.\n\nLFSCK checks layouts and the consistency of MDT and OST objects, not\nfile contents, and that works for the objects of parity components as\nfor those of data components, so accept EC layouts everywhere, and\ndrop the argument of lfsck_layout_verify_header() that selected them.\n\nA repair that gives a component a new empty OST object, for a dangling\nreference with \"lfsck --create-ostobj\" or for an object shared with\nanother file, would leave an EC component without its parity or data.\nA parity component still gets the new object, but is marked stale\nfirst, with the file write pending, so that a resync rewrites it,\nunless no data mirror would then be in sync.  A data component whose\nin-sync parity can rebuild one more stripe gets a dummy slot instead,\nas the orphan handling leaves for a lost object, so that EC reads\nrebuild that stripe from parity, and the object of the other file is\nno longer referenced.  Otherwise it gets the empty object as before.\n\nAdd sanity-lfsck test_55 to read and resync an EC file whose data and\nparity objects name a parent that does not exist, with\nlfsck_verify_pfid enabled, and test_56 to repair an EC file whose data\nand parity objects are all lost.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lfsck\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I35f88d4f3c724061c17af2ae70f614f0003ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
